                                       "kibana.alert.rule.parameters":  {
                                                                            "description":  "Detects a value being written to a Run or RunOnce key, which causes the referenced\ncommand to execute at logon.\n\nThis rule watches a state change rather than a process launch, so it uses Sysmon\nEvent ID 13 (registry value set). It is deliberately written against the registry\npath instead of the value contents, because the payload an attacker stores there is\nunbounded while the small set of autorun locations is not. That trade makes the rule\ndurable but noisy, which is why the tuning note below matters.\n",
